---
description: MVP scope boundary. Applies whenever a task touches framework/compliance mapping, portal integrations, multilingual support, enterprise SSO/RBAC, third-party risk scoring, or fine-tuning from reviewer edits.
alwaysApply: false
---
The following are explicitly post-MVP per `specs/00-overview-and-mvp-scope.md`:

- Automated compliance-framework mapping as a decision layer (FR12 is
  allowed only as a human-confirmed suggestion after finalization).
- ISO 27001 / SOC 2 / GDPR / HIPAA / NIST control mapping as automation.
- Third-party vendor risk scoring.
- Live bidirectional questionnaire-portal integrations.
- Multilingual questionnaires.
- Enterprise SSO/SAML, advanced RBAC, regional production deployment.
- Autonomous fine-tuning from reviewer edits (the Approved-Edit Reuse
  Store is a versioned retrieval exemplar pool, not a training loop).

If a request would implement any of these, don't build it silently —
confirm with the user that they specifically want the post-MVP
extension rather than the MVP-scoped version of the feature, since
scope creep here directly works against the 24-week timeline in
`specs/roadmap-24-week.md`.
